00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:31.840
thousands of Ukrainian refugees refugees. The West&nbsp;
is used to Russia behaving like a malign actor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.920
Over time, it's also widely seen as responsible&nbsp;
for rather. It also sees Russia as responsible for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:47.280
a nerve agent attack on UK soil in 2018 and was&nbsp;
subsequently sanctioned. And it goes on to explain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:53.840
that this may have been, in a sense, the worst&nbsp;
unintended consequence of what Putin is doing now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:59.120
Putin may end up dead at the end of this entire&nbsp;
thing. We don't know. Putin may end up deposed out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:06.160
of power. We don't know. Putin may end up taking&nbsp;
Ukraine. We don't know at this point in time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:13.600
But the way in which this has unified the West&nbsp;
over the long term is not particularly good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.400
for Putin's bigger picture ambitions. Now there's&nbsp;
another aspect to this which we've seen at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

